nearly nothing, year after year.

287
00:08:59,842 --> 00:09:01,339
The problem is inflation.

288
00:09:01,519 --> 00:09:03,261
At three percent inflation,

289
00:09:03,261 --> 00:09:05,455
money loses about a quarter of its

290
00:09:05,455 --> 00:09:07,649
buying power in roughly ten years.

291
00:09:07,829 --> 00:09:10,014
So fifty thousand dollars sitting in a

292
00:09:10,014 --> 00:09:12,313
zero interest account for a decade might

293
00:09:12,313 --> 00:09:14,613
only buy what thirty seven thousand buys

294
00:09:14,613 --> 00:09:14,958
today.

295
00:09:15,138 --> 00:09:17,009
Playing it too safe is its own

296
00:09:17,009 --> 00:09:17,820
kind of risk.

297
00:09:18,170 --> 00:09:20,368
The fix: decide how much you need

298
00:09:20,368 --> 00:09:21,767
as an emergency fund,

299
00:09:21,767 --> 00:09:23,698
and keep that in a high yield

300
00:09:23,698 --> 00:09:24,764
savings account.

301
00:09:24,944 --> 00:09:27,080
Then invest the rest for the long

302
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:29,476
term, gradually if that feels better,

303
00:09:29,476 --> 00:09:31,936
in a diversified mix that matches your

304
00:09:31,936 --> 00:09:34,331
timeline and your stomach for ups and

305
00:09:34,331 --> 00:09:34,720
downs.

306
00:09:35,070 --> 00:09:36,451
Danger number six.

307
00:09:36,631 --> 00:09:39,650
Investing in a friend's or relative's business.

308
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,263
Your cousin is opening a restaurant.

309
00:09:42,443 --> 00:09:44,301
Your friend has an app idea.

310
00:09:44,481 --> 00:09:46,557
They need twenty thousand dollars to get

311
00:09:46,557 --> 00:09:48,011
started, and you have fifty.

312
00:09:48,191 --> 00:09:50,164
Saying no feels selfish.

313
00:09:50,344 --> 00:09:52,074
Saying yes feels generous.

314
00:09:52,254 --> 00:09:54,336
But small businesses are risky,

315
00:09:54,336 --> 00:09:56,821
and a large share don't survive their

316
00:09:56,821 --> 00:09:58,164
first several years,

317
00:09:58,164 --> 00:10:01,119
according to Bureau of Labor Statistics data

318
00:10:01,119 --> 00:10:02,529
on business survival.

319
00:10:02,879 --> 00:10:05,245
And when money and relationships mix,

320
00:10:05,245 --> 00:10:06,396
you can lose both.

321
00:10:06,576 --> 00:10:08,315
If the business struggles,

322
00:10:08,315 --> 00:10:09,854
you may feel resentful,

323
00:10:09,854 --> 00:10:12,463
and they may feel pressured or ashamed.

324
00:10:12,643 --> 00:10:15,610
Some families and friendships never fully recover

325
00:10:15,610 --> 00:10:17,124
from a failed investment.

326
00:10:17,474 --> 00:10:19,222
The fix: if you want to help,

327
00:10:19,222 --> 00:10:21,633
decide on an amount you'd be comfortable

328
00:10:21,633 --> 00:10:22,778
treating as a gift,

329
00:10:22,778 --> 00:10:23,441
not a loan.

330
00:10:23,621 --> 00:10:25,997
Put any real investment in writing,

331
00:10:25,997 --> 00:10:27,151
with clear terms.

332
00:10:27,331 --> 00:10:29,421
And never invest money you need for

333
00:10:29,421 --> 00:10:31,452
your own safety net or retirement.

334
00:10:31,802 --> 00:10:33,055
Danger number seven.

335
00:10:33,235 --> 00:10:35,287
Quitting your job because you finally have

336
00:10:35,287 --> 00:10:35,581
money.

337
00:10:35,931 --> 00:10:38,647
Fifty thousand dollars feels like freedom.

338
00:10:38,827 --> 00:10:40,132
And for some people,

339
00:10:40,132 --> 00:10:41,175
a planned break,

340
00:10:41,175 --> 00:10:43,523
a career change or a business launch

341
00:10:43,523 --> 00:10:44,632
is exactly right.

342
00:10:44,812 --> 00:10:46,941
But many people quit without a plan,

343
00:10:46,941 --> 00:10:48,655
assuming the money will last.

344
00:10:48,835 --> 00:10:51,461
Spending four thousand dollars a month,

345
00:10:51,461 --> 00:10:53,885
fifty thousand lasts about one year.

346
00:10:54,065 --> 00:10:55,650
Add health insurance,

347
00:10:55,650 --> 00:10:57,084
and it goes faster.

348
00:10:57,434 --> 00:10:59,098
And when the money's gone,

349
00:10:59,098 --> 00:11:01,146
people often return to work in a

350
00:11:01,146 --> 00:11:03,514
worse position, with no savings and a

351
00:11:03,514 --> 00:11:04,794
gap on their resume.

352
00:11:04,974 --> 00:11:07,378
The fifty thousand that could have grown

353
00:11:07,378 --> 00:11:08,580
for decades is gone,

354
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:10,083
and they're back at zero.

355
00:11:10,433 --> 00:11:12,384
The fix: if you want to leave,

356
00:11:12,384 --> 00:11:13,556
make a plan first.

357
00:11:13,736 --> 00:11:15,106
How many months will you fund?

358
00:11:15,286 --> 00:11:16,586
What's the goal,

359
00:11:16,586 --> 00:11:17,399
a new job,

360
00:11:17,399 --> 00:11:19,105
a business, a degree?

361
00:11:19,285 --> 00:11:20,989
What's the plan if it doesn't work

362
00:11:20,989 --> 00:11:21,189
out?

363
00:11:21,369 --> 00:11:23,848
Keep part of your money invested and

364
00:11:23,848 --> 00:11:26,740
untouchable, so a break doesn't erase your

365
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:27,360
progress.

366
00:11:27,710 --> 00:11:28,789
Quick pause.

367
00:11:28,969 --> 00:11:30,830
If you're near fifty thousand,

368
00:11:30,830 --> 00:11:32,132
or on your way there,

369
00:11:32,132 --> 00:11:33,683
subscribe to the channel.

370
00:11:33,863 --> 00:11:36,055
I'm building a full series on every

371
00:11:36,055 --> 00:11:38,373
money level, from the first dollar to

372
00:11:38,373 --> 00:11:40,628
one million, and new videos come out

373
00:11:40,628 --> 00:11:41,943
every couple of days.

374
00:11:42,123 --> 00:11:44,120
Okay, danger number eight.

375
00:11:44,471 --> 00:11:45,748
Danger number eight.

376
00:11:45,928 --> 00:11:46,566
Scams.

377
00:11:46,917 --> 00:11:49,726
The Federal Trade Commission has reported that

378
00:11:49,726 --> 00:11:52,596
consumers lost more than twelve billion dollars

379
00:11:52,596 --> 00:11:54,489
to fraud in twenty twenty four,

380
00:11:54,489 --> 00:11:57,725
with investment scams among the costliest categories.

381
00:11:57,905 --> 00:11:59,325
And the more money you have,

382
00:11:59,325 --> 00:12:01,354
the more attractive you are to scammers.

383
00:12:01,703 --> 00:12:03,967
Modern scams are sophisticated.

384
00:12:04,147 --> 00:12:07,754
Fake investment platforms that show impressive gains,

385
00:12:07,754 --> 00:12:09,523
until you try to withdraw.

386
00:12:09,703 --> 00:12:12,536
Romance scams that build trust for months.

387
00:12:12,716 --> 00:12:14,606
Calls pretending to be your bank,

388
00:12:14,606 --> 00:12:16,267
asking you to move money to a

389
00:12:16,267 --> 00:12:17,011
safe account.

390
00:12:17,191 --> 00:12:19,423
People who are smart and careful still

391
00:12:19,423 --> 00:12:20,245
fall for them.

392
00:12:20,595 --> 00:12:23,470
The fix: never move money because someone

393
00:12:23,470 --> 00:12:25,854
contacted you and created urgency.

394
00:12:26,034 --> 00:12:27,792
Hang up and call your bank using

395
00:12:27,792 --> 00:12:29,110
the number on your card.

396
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:32,284
Be suspicious of any investment promising high

397
00:12:32,284 --> 00:12:33,911
returns with little risk.

398
00:12:34,091 --> 00:12:36,143
And talk to someone you trust before

399
00:12:36,143 --> 00:12:37,226
any large transfer.

400
00:12:37,576 --> 00:12:38,899
Danger number nine.

401
00:12:39,079 --> 00:12:40,124
Overconfidence.

402
00:12:40,474 --> 00:12:43,453
Reaching fifty thousand dollars takes discipline,

403
00:12:43,453 --> 00:12:45,338
and it's natural to feel proud.

404
00:12:45,518 --> 00:12:47,991
But pride can turn into overconfidence.

405
00:12:48,171 --> 00:12:50,419
People start believing they have a special

406
00:12:50,419 --> 00:12:51,329
talent for money.

407
00:12:51,509 --> 00:12:52,989
They take bigger risks,

408
00:12:52,989 --> 00:12:54,083
trade more often,

409
00:12:54,083 --> 00:12:56,336
or put money into things they don't

410
00:12:56,336 --> 00:12:57,430
fully understand.

411
00:12:57,779 --> 00:13:01,590
Behavioral finance research has found that overconfident

412
00:13:01,590 --> 00:13:04,040
investors tend to trade too much and

413
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:05,469
diversify too little,

414
00:13:05,469 --> 00:13:07,578
both of which can hurt returns.

415
00:13:07,758 --> 00:13:10,291
Getting to fifty thousand was mostly about

416
00:13:10,291 --> 00:13:11,497
saving consistently.

417
00:13:11,677 --> 00:13:13,778
Growing it to five hundred thousand is

418
00:13:13,778 --> 00:13:16,100
mostly about not interrupting compounding.

419
00:13:16,451 --> 00:13:18,633
The fix: remember what got you here.

420
00:13:18,813 --> 00:13:21,878
Consistent saving, spending less than you earn,

421
00:13:21,878 --> 00:13:22,726
and patience.

422
00:13:22,906 --> 00:13:25,347
Write your investment plan down while you're

423
00:13:25,347 --> 00:13:27,289
calm, including what you'll do in a

424
00:13:27,289 --> 00:13:29,452
market crash, and follow it when you're

425
00:13:29,452 --> 00:13:29,674
not.

426
00:13:30,025 --> 00:13:31,302
Danger number ten.

427
00:13:31,482 --> 00:13:33,490
The wrong financial advisor.

428
00:13:33,841 --> 00:13:35,461
At fifty thousand dollars,

429
00:13:35,461 --> 00:13:38,391
you start getting attention from people selling

430
00:13:38,391 --> 00:13:39,576
financial products.

431
00:13:39,756 --> 00:13:40,933
Some are excellent,

432
00:13:40,933 --> 00:13:43,040
and some are paid by commission on

433
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:43,969
what they sell,

434
00:13:43,969 --> 00:13:46,385
which can create conflicts of interest.

435
00:13:46,565 --> 00:13:48,635
High fee products can quietly eat a

436
00:13:48,635 --> 00:13:50,942
large part of your growth over decades.

437
00:13:51,293 --> 00:13:53,747
A one percent yearly fee doesn't sound

438
00:13:53,747 --> 00:13:54,392
like much.

439
00:13:54,572 --> 00:13:55,939
But over thirty years,

440
00:13:55,939 --> 00:13:58,734
the difference between paying one percent and

441
00:13:58,734 --> 00:14:00,971
paying a small fraction of a percent

442
00:14:00,971 --> 00:14:02,896
can add up to tens of thousands

443
00:14:02,896 --> 00:14:05,133
of dollars, even on a fifty thousand

444
00:14:05,133 --> 00:14:06,623
dollar starting balance,

445
00:14:06,623 --> 00:14:09,108
because fees compound just like returns.

446
00:14:09,458 --> 00:14:11,871
The fix: ask any advisor how they're

447
00:14:11,871 --> 00:14:13,010
paid, in writing.

448
00:14:13,190 --> 00:14:15,081
Look for fee only advisors who are

449
00:14:15,081 --> 00:14:17,695
fiduciaries, meaning they're required to act in

450
00:14:17,695 --> 00:14:18,751
your best interest.

451
00:14:18,931 --> 00:14:21,451
And compare costs in dollars per year,

452
00:14:21,451 --> 00:14:22,844
not just percentages.

453
00:14:23,194 --> 00:14:24,575
Danger number eleven.

454
00:14:24,755 --> 00:14:26,404
Lending money to people you know.

455
00:14:26,754 --> 00:14:29,162
When family and friends know you have

456
00:14:29,162 --> 00:14:30,724
money, requests come in.

457
00:14:30,904 --> 00:14:32,744
Rent help, a car repair,

458
00:14:32,744 --> 00:14:33,894
a medical bill,

459
00:14:33,894 --> 00:14:34,968
a fresh start.

460
00:14:35,148 --> 00:14:36,710
Many of these are real needs,

461
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:38,273
and wanting to help is a good

462
00:14:38,273 --> 00:14:38,596
thing.

463
00:14:38,776 --> 00:14:41,406
But informal loans often don't get paid

464
00:14:41,406 --> 00:14:44,171
back, and asking for repayment can damage

465
00:14:44,171 --> 00:14:45,115
relationships.

466
00:14:45,465 --> 00:14:47,974
Every loan that becomes an unplanned gift

467
00:14:47,974 --> 00:14:49,994
is money that won't grow for your

468
00:14:49,994 --> 00:14:50,422
future.

469
00:14:50,602 --> 00:14:52,811
And once word gets around that you

470
00:14:52,811 --> 00:14:55,281
lend money, requests tend to multiply.

471
00:14:55,631 --> 00:14:57,689
The fix: decide on a yearly helping

472
00:14:57,689 --> 00:14:59,924
budget, an amount you can give without

473
00:14:59,924 --> 00:15:00,983
hurting your plan.

474
00:15:01,163 --> 00:15:02,090
When you help,

475
00:15:02,090 --> 00:15:03,348
consider it a gift,

476
00:15:03,348 --> 00:15:04,077
not a loan.

477
00:15:04,257 --> 00:15:06,059
That way, if it comes back,

478
00:15:06,059 --> 00:15:07,728
it's a pleasant surprise.

479
00:15:07,908 --> 00:15:08,806
If it doesn't,

480
00:15:08,806 --> 00:15:10,474
the relationship survives.

481
00:15:10,824 --> 00:15:12,240
Danger number twelve.

482
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:16,205
Having everything invested and no emergency fund.

483
00:15:16,555 --> 00:15:19,123
Some people invest every dollar of their

484
00:15:19,123 --> 00:15:21,756
fifty thousand, and keep nothing in cash.

485
00:15:21,936 --> 00:15:23,537
Then a job loss or a big

486
00:15:23,537 --> 00:15:25,873
bill arrives during a market crash,

487
00:15:25,873 --> 00:15:28,609
and they're forced to sell investments at

488
00:15:28,609 --> 00:15:29,076
a loss.

489
00:15:29,256 --> 00:15:31,476
That turns a temporary drop into a

490
00:15:31,476 --> 00:15:32,391
permanent one.

491
00:15:32,741 --> 00:15:35,423
Market declines often arrive at the same

492
00:15:35,423 --> 00:15:36,496
time as layoffs,

493
00:15:36,496 --> 00:15:39,045
because both happen during recessions.

494
00:15:39,225 --> 00:15:41,794
That's exactly when you're most likely to

495
00:15:41,794 --> 00:15:44,740
need cash, and exactly when selling investments

496
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:45,680
hurts the most.

497
00:15:46,030 --> 00:15:48,096
The fix: split your money by job.

498
00:15:48,276 --> 00:15:51,021
Three to six months of essential expenses

499
00:15:51,021 --> 00:15:53,164
in a high yield savings account.

500
00:15:53,344 --> 00:15:55,387
The rest invested for the long term.

501
00:15:55,567 --> 00:15:57,996
That way, emergencies never force you to

502
00:15:57,996 --> 00:16:00,060
sell at the worst possible moment.

503
00:16:00,411 --> 00:16:01,908
Danger number thirteen.

504
00:16:02,088 --> 00:16:04,319
Using your fifty thousand to pay off

505
00:16:04,319 --> 00:16:06,860
cheap debt while ignoring better options.

506
00:16:07,210 --> 00:16:08,967
Paying off debt feels great,

507
00:16:08,967 --> 00:16:11,477
and high interest debt should usually go

508
00:16:11,477 --> 00:16:11,854
first.

509
00:16:12,034 --> 00:16:14,493
But some people use all their savings

510
00:16:14,493 --> 00:16:16,421
to pay off low interest debt,

511
00:16:16,421 --> 00:16:18,349
like a mortgage or a car loan

512
00:16:18,349 --> 00:16:19,279
at a low rate,

513
00:16:19,279 --> 00:16:21,938
and leave themselves with no cushion and

514
00:16:21,938 --> 00:16:22,935
no investments.

515
00:16:23,286 --> 00:16:25,295
If your mortgage rate is low and

516
00:16:25,295 --> 00:16:27,116
your emergency fund is empty,

517
00:16:27,116 --> 00:16:29,251
paying it off early might make you

518
00:16:29,251 --> 00:16:30,507
less safe, not more.

519
00:16:30,687 --> 00:16:32,633
You can't easily get that money back

520
00:16:32,633 --> 00:16:34,472
out of your house in an emergency.

521
00:16:34,822 --> 00:16:37,260
The fix: pay off high interest debt

522
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:39,419
first, especially credit cards.

523
00:16:39,599 --> 00:16:41,584
Keep a solid emergency fund.

524
00:16:41,764 --> 00:16:43,390
Get your full employer match.

525
00:16:43,570 --> 00:16:45,891
Then decide about low interest debt,

526
00:16:45,891 --> 00:16:47,116
based on your rate,

527
00:16:47,116 --> 00:16:49,308
your goals, and how you feel about

528
00:16:49,308 --> 00:16:49,630
debt.

529
00:16:49,810 --> 00:16:50,646
Order matters.

530
00:16:50,996 --> 00:16:52,609
Danger number fourteen.

531
00:16:52,789 --> 00:16:53,985
Ignoring taxes.

532
00:16:54,336 --> 00:16:56,768
If your fifty thousand dollars sits in

533
00:16:56,768 --> 00:16:58,432
a regular taxable account,

534
00:16:58,432 --> 00:17:00,737
interest and some gains may be taxed

535
00:17:00,737 --> 00:17:01,441
every year.

536
00:17:01,621 --> 00:17:04,988
If you're not using tax advantaged accounts,

537
00:17:04,988 --> 00:17:05,906
like a 401k,

538
00:17:05,906 --> 00:17:08,507
an IRA or a health savings account

539
00:17:08,507 --> 00:17:11,415
where eligible, you may be paying more

540
00:17:11,415 --> 00:17:13,022
tax than you need to.

541
00:17:13,372 --> 00:17:16,300
And selling investments in a regular account

542
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:18,364
can create capital gains taxes.

543
00:17:18,544 --> 00:17:19,724
Short term gains,

544
00:17:19,724 --> 00:17:21,807
on things held a year or less,

545
00:17:21,807 --> 00:17:24,445
are usually taxed at higher rates than

546
00:17:24,445 --> 00:17:25,556
long term gains.

547
00:17:25,736 --> 00:17:28,742
Frequent trading can quietly raise your tax

548
00:17:28,742 --> 00:17:29,092
bill.

549
00:17:29,442 --> 00:17:32,587
The fix: use tax advantaged accounts first,

550
00:17:32,587 --> 00:17:34,782
within the current IRS limits.

551
00:17:34,962 --> 00:17:37,132
Hold long term investments for more than

552
00:17:37,132 --> 00:17:38,596
a year when it makes sense.

553
00:17:38,776 --> 00:17:41,281
And consider talking to a tax professional

554
00:17:41,281 --> 00:17:43,189
once, to make sure your money is

555
00:17:43,189 --> 00:17:44,442
in the right buckets.

556
00:17:44,792 --> 00:17:46,336
Danger number fifteen.

557
00:17:46,516 --> 00:17:47,352
The biggest one.

558
00:17:47,532 --> 00:17:48,310
Stopping.

559
00:17:48,660 --> 00:17:51,440
Many people reach fifty thousand dollars,

560
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:53,338
feel safe, and stop pushing.

561
00:17:53,518 --> 00:17:55,306
They lower their contributions.

562
00:17:55,486 --> 00:17:56,601
They stop tracking.

563
00:17:56,781 --> 00:17:57,536
They coast.

564
00:17:57,716 --> 00:18:00,007
And because fifty thousand feels like a

565
00:18:00,007 --> 00:18:02,592
lot, they don't notice that they've stalled.

566
00:18:02,942 --> 00:18:06,094
But the difference between stopping and continuing

567
00:18:06,094 --> 00:18:06,599
is huge.

568
00:18:06,779 --> 00:18:09,369
Fifty thousand left alone might become about

569
00:18:09,369 --> 00:18:11,724
four hundred thousand in thirty years at

570
00:18:11,724 --> 00:18:13,431
a seven percent illustration.

571
00:18:13,611 --> 00:18:15,907
Fifty thousand plus five hundred a month

572
00:18:15,907 --> 00:18:17,686
might become about one million.

573
00:18:17,866 --> 00:18:19,981
Keeping the habit going is worth more

574
00:18:19,981 --> 00:18:21,582
than half a million dollars.

575
00:18:21,932 --> 00:18:23,880
The fix: set the next goal before

576
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:25,415
you reach the current one.

577
00:18:25,595 --> 00:18:27,076
When you hit fifty thousand,

578
00:18:27,076 --> 00:18:28,980
you should already be aiming for one

579
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:29,879
hundred thousand.

580
00:18:30,059 --> 00:18:32,441
Keep your automatic contributions running,

581
00:18:32,441 --> 00:18:34,539
and raise them every time your income

582
00:18:34,539 --> 00:18:34,993
goes up.

583
00:18:35,343 --> 00:18:37,212
Let's see these dangers play out.

584
00:18:37,392 --> 00:18:38,817
Three example people,

585
00:18:38,817 --> 00:18:41,464
each with fifty thousand dollars at age

586
00:18:41,464 --> 00:18:42,210
thirty two.

587
00:18:42,390 --> 00:18:43,338
They're made up,

588
00:18:43,338 --> 00:18:45,115
but each path is one that real

589
00:18:45,115 --> 00:18:46,419
people take every day.

590
00:18:46,769 --> 00:18:48,290
Person one, Ethan.

591
00:18:48,470 --> 00:18:51,129
Ethan has fifty thousand dollars and a

592
00:18:51,129 --> 00:18:53,439
car that runs fine but feels old.

593
00:18:53,619 --> 00:18:55,553
He buys a new truck for forty

594
00:18:55,553 --> 00:18:57,288
eight thousand, pays cash,

595
00:18:57,288 --> 00:18:58,356
and feels great.

596
00:18:58,536 --> 00:19:00,255
Over the next few years,

597
00:19:00,255 --> 00:19:02,907
he upgrades his apartment and takes a

598
00:19:02,907 --> 00:19:04,770
couple of expensive trips.

599
00:19:04,950 --> 00:19:06,485
He keeps saving a little,

600
00:19:06,485 --> 00:19:07,713
but there's no plan.

601
00:19:07,893 --> 00:19:08,997
Ten years later,

602
00:19:08,997 --> 00:19:11,203
the truck is worth a fraction of

603
00:19:11,203 --> 00:19:12,100
what he paid,

604
00:19:12,100 --> 00:19:15,341
and Ethan's savings are around fifteen thousand

605
00:19:15,341 --> 00:19:15,893
dollars.

606
00:19:16,073 --> 00:19:18,358
He's forty two and almost back where

607
00:19:18,358 --> 00:19:19,056
he started.

608
00:19:19,407 --> 00:19:21,137
Person two, Sofia.

609
00:19:21,317 --> 00:19:23,530
Sofia was so nervous about losing her

610
00:19:23,530 --> 00:19:25,564
fifty thousand that she left it in

611
00:19:25,564 --> 00:19:26,820
her checking account.

612
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,280
She kept saving,

613
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:31,241
adding three hundred dollars a month,

614
00:19:31,241 --> 00:19:32,201
all in cash.

615
00:19:32,381 --> 00:19:33,415
Ten years later,

616
00:19:33,415 --> 00:19:36,131
she has about eighty six thousand dollars.

617
00:19:36,311 --> 00:19:37,364
That sounds good,

618
00:19:37,364 --> 00:19:39,594
but inflation has eaten a large part

619
00:19:39,594 --> 00:19:40,834
of its buying power,

620
00:19:40,834 --> 00:19:43,064
and she missed a decade of potential

621
00:19:43,064 --> 00:19:43,498
growth.

622
00:19:43,678 --> 00:19:46,536
She's safe, but she's falling behind without

623
00:19:46,536 --> 00:19:47,381
realizing it.

624
00:19:47,731 --> 00:19:49,519
Person three, Marcus.

625
00:19:49,699 --> 00:19:51,696
Marcus keeps his old car.

626
00:19:51,876 --> 00:19:54,392
He sets aside fifteen thousand as an

627
00:19:54,392 --> 00:19:57,119
emergency fund in a high yield account,

628
00:19:57,119 --> 00:20:00,055
and invests the other thirty five thousand

629
00:20:00,055 --> 00:20:01,732
in low cost index funds.

630
00:20:01,912 --> 00:20:04,288
He adds five hundred dollars a month,

631
00:20:04,288 --> 00:20:05,186
automatically.

632
00:20:05,366 --> 00:20:06,879
He ignores the hot tips,

633
00:20:06,879 --> 00:20:09,275
says no to a friend's restaurant idea,

634
00:20:09,275 --> 00:20:11,671
and keeps going through a market drop.

635
00:20:11,851 --> 00:20:13,984
At a seven percent illustration,

636
00:20:13,984 --> 00:20:16,851
his investments could be around one hundred

637
00:20:16,851 --> 00:20:19,852
fifty seven thousand dollars after ten years,

638
00:20:19,852 --> 00:20:21,452
plus his emergency fund.

639
00:20:21,802 --> 00:20:23,323
Same starting point.

640
00:20:23,503 --> 00:20:24,547
Same age.

641
00:20:24,727 --> 00:20:25,803
Ten years later,

642
00:20:25,803 --> 00:20:28,022
Ethan has about fifteen thousand,

643
00:20:28,022 --> 00:20:30,174
Sofia about eighty six thousand,

644
00:20:30,174 --> 00:20:33,335
and Marcus around one hundred seventy thousand,

645
00:20:33,335 --> 00:20:34,747
counting his cushion.

646
00:20:34,927 --> 00:20:37,057
And the gap keeps widening every year

647
00:20:37,057 --> 00:20:37,690
after that.

648
00:20:37,870 --> 00:20:40,784
Nobody in this story did anything crazy.

649
00:20:40,964 --> 00:20:42,381
Ethan bought a truck.

650
00:20:42,561 --> 00:20:43,977
Sofia was careful.

651
00:20:44,157 --> 00:20:45,608
Marcus was boring.

652
00:20:45,788 --> 00:20:46,508
Boring won.

653
00:20:46,858 --> 00:20:48,680
Now let's put some numbers on the

654
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:49,122
choices.

655
00:20:49,302 --> 00:20:52,128
Here's what fifty thousand dollars could become

656
00:20:52,128 --> 00:20:53,210
over thirty years,

657
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:55,014
depending on what you do next.

658
00:20:55,194 --> 00:20:57,867
All of these use simple illustrations,

659
00:20:57,867 --> 00:20:58,781
not promises.

660
00:20:59,131 --> 00:21:00,152
Scenario one.

661
00:21:00,332 --> 00:21:01,052
Spend it.

662
00:21:01,232 --> 00:21:02,739
A car, a wedding,

663
00:21:02,739 --> 00:21:03,891
a renovation.

664
00:21:04,071 --> 00:21:04,996
In thirty years,

665
00:21:04,996 --> 00:21:07,831
that fifty thousand is worth nothing financially,

666
00:21:07,831 --> 00:21:09,739
though you may have memories or a

667
00:21:09,739 --> 00:21:10,549
nicer kitchen.

668
00:21:10,729 --> 00:21:12,691
Sometimes that's a fine choice.

669
00:21:12,871 --> 00:21:14,044
Just make it knowingly.

670
00:21:14,224 --> 00:21:15,582
Scenario two.

671
00:21:15,762 --> 00:21:18,015
Leave it in cash at no interest.

672
00:21:18,195 --> 00:21:19,326
Thanks to inflation,

673
00:21:19,326 --> 00:21:21,476
its buying power in thirty years could

674
00:21:21,476 --> 00:21:23,061
be less than half of what it

675
00:21:23,061 --> 00:21:23,570
is today.

676
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,301
Scenario three.

677
00:21:25,481 --> 00:21:28,186
Invest it and never add another dollar.

678
00:21:28,366 --> 00:21:29,556
At seven percent,

679
00:21:29,556 --> 00:21:32,635
roughly four hundred six thousand dollars in

680
00:21:32,635 --> 00:21:33,544
thirty years.

681
00:21:33,724 --> 00:21:34,851
Scenario four.

682
00:21:35,031 --> 00:21:37,240
Invest it and add five hundred a

683
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:37,654
month.

684
00:21:37,834 --> 00:21:39,971
Roughly one million dollars.

685
00:21:40,151 --> 00:21:41,428
Scenario five.

686
00:21:41,608 --> 00:21:43,856
Invest it and add one thousand a

687
00:21:43,856 --> 00:21:44,278
month.

688
00:21:44,458 --> 00:21:47,082
Roughly one point six million dollars.

689
00:21:47,262 --> 00:21:48,678
Same fifty thousand.

690
00:21:48,858 --> 00:21:50,356
Wildly different futures.

691
00:21:50,706 --> 00:21:52,435
The lesson isn't that you can never

692
00:21:52,435 --> 00:21:53,028
spend money.

693
00:21:53,208 --> 00:21:54,863
It's that at fifty thousand,

694
00:21:54,863 --> 00:21:57,051
every big decision has a long shadow.

695
00:21:57,231 --> 00:21:59,831
A forty thousand dollar purchase today isn't

696
00:21:59,831 --> 00:22:01,782
a forty thousand dollar decision.

697
00:22:01,962 --> 00:22:03,013
Over thirty years,

698
00:22:03,013 --> 00:22:05,114
it could be a three hundred thousand

699
00:22:05,114 --> 00:22:06,048
dollar decision.

700
00:22:06,228 --> 00:22:08,146
Knowing that doesn't mean saying no to

701
00:22:08,146 --> 00:22:08,701
everything.

702
00:22:08,881 --> 00:22:10,611
It means saying yes only to the

703
00:22:10,611 --> 00:22:12,341
things that are truly worth it.

704
00:22:12,691 --> 00:22:13,573
Angle two.

705
00:22:13,753 --> 00:22:14,891
The psychology.

706
00:22:15,071 --> 00:22:17,662
Why is fifty thousand dollars so dangerous

707
00:22:17,662 --> 00:22:19,390
for our brains specifically?

708
00:22:19,740 --> 00:22:22,424
The first reason is what psychologists call

709
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:23,548
the wealth effect.

710
00:22:23,728 --> 00:22:25,280
When people feel richer,

711
00:22:25,280 --> 00:22:26,833
they tend to spend more,

712
00:22:26,833 --> 00:22:29,161
even if their income hasn't changed.

713
00:22:29,341 --> 00:22:31,385
Seeing a big number in your account

714
00:22:31,385 --> 00:22:33,312
makes larger purchases feel safe.

715
00:22:33,492 --> 00:22:34,708
That feeling is real,

716
00:22:34,708 --> 00:22:35,867
but it's misleading,

717
00:22:35,867 --> 00:22:38,127
because fifty thousand dollars is not a

718
00:22:38,127 --> 00:22:39,343
lot of yearly income.

719
00:22:39,693 --> 00:22:42,221
The second reason is mental accounting,

720
00:22:42,221 --> 00:22:44,685
an idea from economist Richard Thaler.

721
00:22:44,865 --> 00:22:47,252
We treat money differently depending on where

722
00:22:47,252 --> 00:22:48,897
it came from and what bucket we

723
00:22:48,897 --> 00:22:49,428
put it in.

724
00:22:49,608 --> 00:22:51,949
A bonus or a tax refund feels

725
00:22:51,949 --> 00:22:53,160
like fun money.

726
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:56,001
A savings balance that's grown big feels

727
00:22:56,001 --> 00:22:57,996
like it's allowed to be spent.

728
00:22:58,176 --> 00:22:59,209
But money is money.

729
00:22:59,389 --> 00:23:01,571
A dollar from a bonus grows just

730
00:23:01,571 --> 00:23:03,547
as well as a dollar from your

731
00:23:03,547 --> 00:23:04,161
paycheck.

732
00:23:04,511 --> 00:23:07,059
The third reason is that fifty thousand

733
00:23:07,059 --> 00:23:09,346
is just big enough to buy something

734
00:23:09,346 --> 00:23:09,607
big.

735
00:23:09,787 --> 00:23:12,216
Ten thousand dollars can't buy a new

736
00:23:12,216 --> 00:23:13,363
truck or a house.

737
00:23:13,543 --> 00:23:15,500
A million dollars is so much that

738
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:17,456
one purchase doesn't make a dent.

739
00:23:17,636 --> 00:23:19,812
But fifty thousand is right at the

740
00:23:19,812 --> 00:23:22,373
size of a single life changing purchase.

741
00:23:22,553 --> 00:23:25,141
That makes the temptation stronger than at

742
00:23:25,141 --> 00:23:26,558
almost any other level.

743
00:23:26,908 --> 00:23:28,846
The fourth reason is the end of

744
00:23:28,846 --> 00:23:29,346
urgency.

745
00:23:29,526 --> 00:23:30,909
Before fifty thousand,

746
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:33,171
many people were saving out of fear.

747
00:23:33,351 --> 00:23:35,082
Fear of emergencies,

748
00:23:35,082 --> 00:23:36,207
fear of debt.

749
00:23:36,387 --> 00:23:37,912
Once they have a cushion,

750
00:23:37,912 --> 00:23:39,071
the fear goes away,

751
00:23:39,071 --> 00:23:40,718
and so does the motivation.

752
00:23:40,898 --> 00:23:42,741
That's why it's so important to replace

753
00:23:42,741 --> 00:23:43,545
fear with a goal.

754
00:23:43,725 --> 00:23:45,130
Not, I need money.

755
00:23:45,310 --> 00:23:47,915
But, I want to be financially independent

756
00:23:47,915 --> 00:23:48,804
by fifty five.

757
00:23:49,155 --> 00:23:50,838
And the fifth is social.

758
00:23:51,018 --> 00:23:53,338
When people around you notice you're doing

759
00:23:53,338 --> 00:23:55,217
well, there's pressure to show it,

760
00:23:55,217 --> 00:23:56,045
or to share it.

761
00:23:56,225 --> 00:23:58,306
Bigger house, nicer car,

762
00:23:58,306 --> 00:24:00,126
more expensive gifts.

763
00:24:00,306 --> 00:24:03,032
Remember the research in The Millionaire Next

764
00:24:03,032 --> 00:24:06,425
Door: many real millionaires looked completely ordinary.

765
00:24:06,605 --> 00:24:08,160
Not showing your wealth is one of

766
00:24:08,160 --> 00:24:09,716
the best ways to keep it growing.

767
00:24:10,066 --> 00:24:11,738
How do you know if fifty thousand

768
00:24:11,738 --> 00:24:13,967
dollars is starting to change your behavior?

769
00:24:14,147 --> 00:24:16,085
Here are six warning signs.

770
00:24:16,265 --> 00:24:17,985
If you notice two or more,

771
00:24:17,985 --> 00:24:20,300
it's time to pause and revisit your

772
00:24:20,300 --> 00:24:20,631
plan.

773
00:24:20,981 --> 00:24:21,642
Sign one.

774
00:24:21,822 --> 00:24:23,541
You've started browsing cars,

775
00:24:23,541 --> 00:24:25,555
houses or big trips much more than

776
00:24:25,555 --> 00:24:28,161
before, and telling yourself you deserve it.

777
00:24:28,341 --> 00:24:28,899
You might.

778
00:24:29,079 --> 00:24:31,131
But notice that the browsing started when

779
00:24:31,131 --> 00:24:31,981
the balance grew.

780
00:24:32,161 --> 00:24:32,962
Sign two.

781
00:24:33,142 --> 00:24:35,299
You've stopped tracking your spending,

782
00:24:35,299 --> 00:24:37,682
because it doesn't feel necessary anymore.

783
00:24:37,862 --> 00:24:40,985
That's exactly when lifestyle creep sneaks in.

784
00:24:41,335 --> 00:24:42,310
Sign three.

785
00:24:42,490 --> 00:24:45,019
You've lowered or paused your automatic savings,

786
00:24:45,019 --> 00:24:47,389
telling yourself you've saved enough for now.

787
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:48,394
Sign four.

788
00:24:48,574 --> 00:24:50,950
You've found yourself excited about a single

789
00:24:50,950 --> 00:24:53,109
investment that could change everything,

790
00:24:53,109 --> 00:24:55,215
and you're thinking about putting a big

791
00:24:55,215 --> 00:24:56,619
chunk of your money in it.

792
00:24:56,799 --> 00:24:58,766
Excitement is a warning light,

793
00:24:58,766 --> 00:24:59,946
not a green light.

794
00:25:00,296 --> 00:25:01,352
Sign five.

795
00:25:01,532 --> 00:25:03,430
Someone has asked you for money,

796
00:25:03,430 --> 00:25:04,676
or for an investment,

797
00:25:04,676 --> 00:25:06,455
and you feel guilty saying no.

798
00:25:06,635 --> 00:25:08,859
That guilt can lead to decisions you'll

799
00:25:08,859 --> 00:25:09,259
regret.

800
00:25:09,439 --> 00:25:11,302
Decide your rules in advance,

801
00:25:11,302 --> 00:25:13,423
so you don't have to decide under

802
00:25:13,423 --> 00:25:14,001
pressure.

803
00:25:14,181 --> 00:25:15,435
And sign six.

804
00:25:15,615 --> 00:25:17,738
You're thinking about quitting your job,

805
00:25:17,738 --> 00:25:19,488
but you don't have a written plan

806
00:25:19,488 --> 00:25:20,550
for what comes next.

807
00:25:20,900 --> 00:25:22,748
None of these signs mean you're doing

808
00:25:22,748 --> 00:25:23,547
something wrong.

809
00:25:23,727 --> 00:25:26,248
They're normal human reactions to having more

810
00:25:26,248 --> 00:25:27,256
money than before.

811
00:25:27,436 --> 00:25:29,329
The point is to notice them early.

812
00:25:29,509 --> 00:25:30,770
A five minute pause,

813
00:25:30,770 --> 00:25:32,789
and a look at your written plan,

814
00:25:32,789 --> 00:25:34,745
can save you years of progress.

815
00:25:34,925 --> 00:25:37,373
That's the difference between people who pass

816
00:25:37,373 --> 00:25:39,441
through the danger zone and people who

817
00:25:39,441 --> 00:25:40,312
get stuck in it.

818
00:25:40,662 --> 00:25:41,579
Angle three.

819
00:25:41,759 --> 00:25:42,455
The playbook.

820
00:25:42,635 --> 00:25:44,287
You have fifty thousand dollars,

821
00:25:44,287 --> 00:25:45,526
or you're getting close.

822
00:25:45,706 --> 00:25:47,370
Here's what to do with it,

823
00:25:47,370 --> 00:25:48,202
step by step.

824
00:25:48,553 --> 00:25:49,307
Step one.

825
00:25:49,487 --> 00:25:51,101
Wipe out high interest debt.

826
00:25:51,281 --> 00:25:53,789
Any credit card or personal loan above

827
00:25:53,789 --> 00:25:56,297
about eight to ten percent goes first.

828
00:25:56,477 --> 00:25:58,725
Paying off a card at twenty percent

829
00:25:58,725 --> 00:26:01,167
is a guaranteed twenty percent return,

830
00:26:01,167 --> 00:26:04,058
and nothing in investing reliably beats that.

831
00:26:04,408 --> 00:26:05,545
Step two.

832
00:26:05,725 --> 00:26:07,722
Set aside your emergency fund.

833
00:26:07,902 --> 00:26:10,815
Three to six months of essential expenses,

834
00:26:10,815 --> 00:26:13,034
in a high yield savings account.

835
00:26:13,214 --> 00:26:15,756
Say your essentials are three thousand dollars

836
00:26:15,756 --> 00:26:16,198
a month.

837
00:26:16,378 --> 00:26:18,328
That's nine to eighteen thousand.

838
00:26:18,508 --> 00:26:20,526
This money is not for investing,

839
00:26:20,526 --> 00:26:21,409
not for a car,

840
00:26:21,409 --> 00:26:22,607
not for a vacation.

841
00:26:22,787 --> 00:26:24,424
It's insurance for your plan.

842
00:26:24,774 --> 00:26:25,714
Step three.

843
00:26:25,894 --> 00:26:27,194
Max out the free money.

844
00:26:27,374 --> 00:26:29,760
Make sure you're getting your full employer

845
00:26:29,760 --> 00:26:31,647
match on retirement contributions.

846
00:26:31,827 --> 00:26:33,626
Then consider an IRA.

847
00:26:33,806 --> 00:26:36,275
Use tax advantaged accounts first,

848
00:26:36,275 --> 00:26:38,454
within the current IRS limits,

849
00:26:38,454 --> 00:26:41,794
before investing in a regular taxable account.

850
00:26:42,144 --> 00:26:42,875
Step four.

851
00:26:43,055 --> 00:26:44,576
Invest the rest simply.

852
00:26:44,756 --> 00:26:47,629
A diversified mix of low cost index

853
00:26:47,629 --> 00:26:50,584
funds, or a single target date fund.

854
00:26:50,764 --> 00:26:53,013
Decide how much goes into stocks and

855
00:26:53,013 --> 00:26:54,262
how much into bonds,

856
00:26:54,262 --> 00:26:56,510
based on your timeline and how you'd

857
00:26:56,510 --> 00:26:57,510
feel in a crash.

858
00:26:57,690 --> 00:27:00,584
Then automate a monthly contribution on top,

859
00:27:00,584 --> 00:27:01,834
